+==== Decision overview
+
+The following flowchart summarizes how esmini decides an object's shape and dimensions:
+
+[mermaid,format="svg"]
+....
+flowchart TD
+    A[OpenDRIVE object] --> B{radius specified?}
+    B -- "yes, no length/width" --> C["Cylinder, length = width = 2 x radius"]
+    B -- "yes, with length/width" --> D["Ignore radius, warn, use length/width"]
+    B -- no --> E{outline defined?}
+    E -- yes --> F{corner type}
+    F -- cornerRoad --> G[Outline follows road curvature]
+    F -- cornerLocal --> H[Rigid local-frame outline]
+    E -- no --> I{3D model found?}
+    I -- yes --> J[Use model bounding box]
+    I -- no --> K[Box / cylinder primitive]
+
+    C --> L{dimension specified?}
+    D --> L
+    J --> L
+    K --> L
+    G --> M{repeat defined?}
+    H --> M
+
+    L -- yes --> N[Scale axis to specified value]
+    L -- "no, model present" --> O[Use model native size for that axis]
+    L -- "no, no model" --> P[Fallback minimum 0.05 m]
+
+    N --> M
+    O --> M
+    P --> M
+    M -- "distance greater than 0" --> Q["Discrete copies along s, params interpolated start to end"]
+    M -- "distance = 0" --> R[Continuous outline along road]
+    M -- "no repeat" --> S[Single instance]
+....
+
+==== OSI mapping
+
+OpenDRIVE (odr) https://publications.pages.asam.net/standards/ASAM_OpenDRIVE/ASAM_OpenDRIVE_Specification/1.8.0/specification/13_objects/13_01_introduction.html[road objects] will be emitted on OSI as https://opensimulationinterface.github.io/osi-antora-generator/asamosi/latest/gen/structosi3_1_1StationaryObject.html[stationary objects]. The OSI https://opensimulationinterface.github.io/osi-antora-generator/asamosi/latest/gen/structosi3_1_1StationaryObject_1_1Classification.html#ad497488a7119617633b54181ea08457d[type] will be based on odr road object https://publications.pages.asam.net/standards/ASAM_OpenDRIVE/ASAM_OpenDRIVE_Specification/1.8.0/specification/16_annexes/enumerations/map_uml_enumerations.html#top-EAID_C47587D0_7173_42df_8BB7_36B2C598D95F[type] and subtype (generic string) as follows:
+
+1. The OpenDRIVE object types `pole`, `tree`, `vegetation`, `barrier`, `building`, and `bridge` map directly to their corresponding OSI stationary-object types.
+2. A `parkingSpace` maps to `TYPE_OTHER` with concrete, solid, grey classification properties. Its parking restrictions are added to the source reference as `restrictions:<value>`.
+3. For all remaining object types, esmini tries to map the subtype to an OSI stationary-object type. The subtype comparison is case-insensitive; `TYPE_` is prepended when it is not already present. For example, subtype `speed_bump` maps to `TYPE_SPEED_BUMP`.
+4. If the subtype does not map, the known OpenDRIVE object types `obstacle`, `railing`, `patch`, `trafficIsland`, `crosswalk`, `streetLamp`, `gantry`, `soundBarrier`, `wind`, and `roadMark` map to `TYPE_OTHER`.
+5. Any other unsupported object type maps to `TYPE_UNKNOWN`.
+
+This schema overcomes limitations from OpenDRIVE and OSI type incompatibility. For example it allows for emitting TYPE_DELINEATOR which has no corresponding road object type:
+
+``         <object type="obstacle" subtype="delineator" name="road_delineator" id="9" s="160" t="4" zOffset="0.0"/>
+``
+
+Each resolved repeat instance of a road object is emitted as a separate OSI stationary object. The first instance uses the object's global ID; additional instances receive new global IDs.
+
+=== Expressions
+From OpenSCENARIO v1.1 https://www.asam.net/index.php?eID=dumpFile&t=f&f=4908&token=ae9d9b44ab9257e817072a653b5d5e98ee0babf8#_expressions[expressions] including mathematical operations are supported in assignment of value to OpenSCENARIO https://www.asam.net/index.php?eID=dumpFile&t=f&f=4908&token=ae9d9b44ab9257e817072a653b5d5e98ee0babf8#_parameters[parameters] and XML element attributes. Examples:
+
+[source,xml]
+----
+<ParameterDeclaration name="PI" parameterType="double" value="3.14159"/>
+<ParameterDeclaration name="KPH2MPS" parameterType="double" value="1/3.6"/>
+
+...
+
+<Position>
+    <LanePosition roadId="1" laneId="-1" s="40" offset="0">
+        <Orientation type="absolute" h="${sin(0.25*$PI)}"/>
+    </LanePosition>
+</Position>
+
+...
+
+<SpeedActionTarget>
+    <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="${110 * $KPH2MPS}"/>
+</SpeedActionTarget>
+----
+
+h and (speed value) evaluates to 0.707106 and 30.55558 respectively
